 "style-guide", "styleguide"], "trees_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/ruff/git/trees{/sha}", "updated_at": "2026-10-26T08:30:10Z", "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/ruff", "visibility": "public", "watchers": 50294, "watchers_count": 50294, "web_commit_signoff_required": false}, "sha": "ce43dbab5828b3e88feb68ebd6f28f3744f8f8c3", "user": {"avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/115962839?v=4", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/astral-sh/events{/privacy}", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/astral-sh/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/astral-sh/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/astral-sh/gists{/gist_id}", "gravatar_id": "", "html_url": "https://github.com/astral-sh", "id": 115962839, "login": "astral-sh", "node_id": "O_kgDOBulz1w", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/astral-sh/orgs", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/astral-sh/received_events", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/astral-sh/repos", "site_admin": false, "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/astral-sh/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/astral-sh/subscriptions", "type": "Organization", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/astral-sh", "user_view_type": "public"}}, "body": "Summary\r\n--\r\n\r\nI thought that emitting multiple diagnostics at once would be difficult to port to a diagnostic construction model closer to ty's `InferContext::report_lint`, so as a first step toward that, this PR removes `Checker::report_diagnostics`.\r\n\r\nIn many cases I was able to do some related refactoring to avoid allocating a `Vec<Diagnostic>` at all, often by adding a `Checker` field to a `Visitor` or by passing a `Checker` instead of a `&mut Vec<Diagnostic>`.\r\n\r\nIn other cases, I had to fall back on something like\r\n\r\n```rust\r\nfor diagnostic in diagnostics {\r\n    checker.report_diagnostic(diagnostic);\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nwhich I guess is a bit worse than the `extend` call in `report_diagnostics`, but hopefully it won't make too much of a difference.\r\n\r\nI'm still not quite sure what to do with the remaining loop cases. The two main use cases for collecting a sequence of diagnostics before emitting any of them are:\r\n\r\n1. Applying a single `Fix` to a group of diagnostics\r\n2. Avoiding an earlier diagnostic if something goes wrong later\r\n\r\nI was hoping we could get away with just a `DiagnosticGuard` that reported a `Diagnostic` on drop, but I guess we will still need a `DiagnosticGuardBuilder` that can be collected in these cases and produce a `DiagnosticGuard` once we know we actually want the diagnostics.\r\n\r\nTest Plan\r\n--\r\n\r\nExisting tests\r\n", "changed_files": 27, "closed_at": "2025-05-20T14:00:07Z", "comments": 1, "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/ruff/issues/18206/comments", "commits": 2, "commits_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/ruff/pulls/18206/commits", "created_at": "2025-05-19T20:34:08Z", "deletions": 366, "diff_url": "https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/18206.diff", "draft": false, "head": {"label": "astral-sh:brent/remove-report-diagnostics", "ref": "brent/remove-report-diagnostics", "repo": {"allow_forking": true, "archive_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/ruff/{archive_format}{/ref}", "archived": false, "assignees_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/ruff/assignees{/user}", "blobs_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/ruff/git/blobs{/sha}", "branches_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/ruff/branches{/branch}", "clone_url": "https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff.git", "collaborators_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/ruff/collaborators{/collaborator}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/ruff/comments{/number}", "commits_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/ruff/commits{/sha}", "compare_url": "https://api.github.com/repos